Here is the commit message:
HADOOP-13189. FairCallQueue makes callQueue larger than the
 configured capacity. Contributed by Vinitha Gankidi.

Here is the root cause:
The bug was caused by the FairCallQueue not properly enforcing the total capacity of all sub-queues, leading to a situation where the combined size of the sub-queues could exceed the configured capacity. This was due to a misunderstanding in the implementation of how the capacity was distributed among the sub-queues, which did not account for the excess capacity of the first sub-queue.

